---
title: Binary space partition rooms
---
Rooms placed in ever-smaller parts of the map, so they come out better spaced than random rooms [[t:61-64 s:7]].

## The rule
```text
start a list with one rectangle and its four quarters
repeat for a fixed number of attempts:
    pick any rectangle on the list
    try a room near its top-left corner
    if it fits: carve it, and add that rectangle's four quarters to the list
sort and join the rooms, as random rooms are
```

The talk describes halving the map, then each half, until a piece is about the size of a room [[t:66-68]]. Its demo is looser: it cuts into quarters, keeps every rectangle it has cut on its list, and quarters a rectangle again each time a room lands in it [[c02:41-55 c02:86-112]].

